(a) 3 benefits: Independent deployability — each service can be deployed/updated without touching others. Independent scalability — scale only the overloaded service (e.g. ProductModule) rather than the whole app. Technology flexibility — each service can use a different stack, database, or language best suited to its needs.
(b) 2 challenges: Distributed system complexity — network latency, partial failures, and eventual consistency are harder to handle than in-process calls. Operational overhead — you now need service discovery, API gateway, distributed tracing, and container orchestration.
(c) Eureka + API Gateway flow: Each service registers itself with Eureka on startup, advertising its name and IP. The API Gateway (also a Eureka client) looks up service locations dynamically. The React frontend only knows one URL (the gateway). When it calls /api/orders/*, the gateway resolves "order-service" via Eureka and routes the request — the frontend never needs to know individual service addresses.